I have the complete chain. Here is the full analysis.

## Overview

POST `/api/owners` is served by `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner(...)`. The path is defined in the generated `OwnersApi` interface (`PATH_ADD_OWNER = "/owners"`, class-level `@RequestMapping("/api")` on the controller → `/api/owners`), method `POST`, consumes/produces `application/json`. There are NO JPA lifecycle callbacks (`@PrePersist`/`@PostPersist`), no `@EntityListeners`, and no `ApplicationEventPublisher` anywhere in the project (grep returned nothing). The only "event" emitted is an SLF4J audit log line. Active persistence profile is `spring-data-jpa` (`src/main/resources/application.properties:20`), so `saveOwner` goes through a Spring Data `Repository` proxy (`SpringDataOwnerRepository`) backed by `SimpleJpaRepository.save`.

---

## 1. The controller method (POST /api/owners)

`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`

Class declaration and security (lines 75-78, 158-159):
- `@RestController`, `@RequestMapping("/api")`, `implements OwnersApi`
- Method guarded by `@PreAuthorize("hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)")` (line 183)

The method itself, `addOwner` (lines 183-229) — this is the core orchestration:

```java
183  @PreAuthorize("hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)")
184  @Override
185  public ResponseEntity<OwnerDto> addOwner(OwnerFieldsDto ownerFieldsDto) {
186      if (ownerFieldsDto != null) {
187          ownerFieldsDto.setAddress(addressNormalizer.normalize(ownerFieldsDto.getAddress()));
188      }
189      List<String> missingFields = ownerFieldsValidator.findMissingOrBlankFields(ownerFieldsDto);
190      if (!missingFields.isEmpty()) {
191          throw new MissingOwnerFieldsException(missingFields);
192      }
193      HttpHeaders headers = new HttpHeaders();
194      Owner owner = ownerMapper.toOwner(ownerFieldsDto);
195      Collection<Owner> sameLastName =
196          this.clinicService.findOwnersByLastNameIgnoreCase(owner.getLastName());
197      owner.setNamesakeCount(namesakeCounter.count(owner, sameLastName));
198      List<Owner> householdMembers = assignHousehold(owner, sameLastName);
199      owner.setTelephone(telephoneNormalizer.normalize(owner.getTelephone()));
200      owner.setEmail(emailNormalizer.normalize(owner.getEmail()));
201      disposableEmailDomainValidator.validate(owner.getEmail());
